[
  {
    "sha": "9af967e38e2fcee556681efcb4d1f42bfa85d743",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDlhZjk2N2UzOGUyZmNlZTU1NjY4MWVmY2I0ZDFmNDJiZmE4NWQ3NDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T19:08:13Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T19:08:13Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): start and exit picks for the 5-axis parallel\n\nA start pick chooses the raster corner where the cut starts (an end of\nthe first or the last pass); an exit pick chooses where the last pass\nends. The passes keep their geometry; only their order and direction\nchange, before the raster's own link laws plan the links. A pick far\nfrom every corner, and an exit that the start's order cannot end at,\nare refused by name. No pick keeps the automatic raster byte for byte.\n\nRefs #3330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "ff660ddb35c23b8d1d0743e5fba3793e6a9e78f5",
